["{

"claim_text": "Hello, This is Stephanie Clark writing about an accident I had yesterday in the grocery store parking lot. A truck backed into my Honda Accord (the 2020 model—VIN 12039485762194836 if you need it). My car is valued at about $19,500 according to my insurer’s last appraisal.\nMy auto policy is POL-573882014, which started last October 1 and runs until the end of September this year. Hopefully that means I’m still covered—I’ve been careful about renewals. This claim should be under reference CLM-624817.\nThe damage is mostly cosmetic—rear bumper dented, scratches across the trunk—but the repair shop quoted $3,100 to $3,200 depending on labor. The exact figure was $3,172, which I wrote down. I also filed a police report; they gave me the number PR-20250911-9821.\nFor context, I was parked at the Safeway lot, row D, while grabbing groceries. A bystander helped me exchange info with the other driver. I also mentioned it to my neighbor, but she kept confusing it with the accident she had last year, so ignore her version of events.\nLet me know what documents you need from me.\nThanks,\nStephanie",

"claim": {
    "header": {
        "claim_id": "CLM-624817",
        "report_date": "2025-09-12",
        "incident_date": "2025-09-12",
        "reported_by": "Stephanie Clark",
        "channel": "Email"
    },
    "policy_details": {
        "policy_number": "POL-573882014",
        "policyholder_name": "Stephanie Clark",
        "coverage_type": "Auto",
        "effective_date": "2020-10-01",
        "expiration_date": "2025-09-30"
    },
    "insured_objects": [
        {
            "object_id": "12039485762194836",
            "object_type": "Vehicle",
            "make_model": "Honda",
            "year": 2020,
            "location_address": "Safeway lot, row D",
            "estimated_value": 19500
        }
    ],
    "incident_description": {
        "incident_type": "Accident",
        "location_type": "Parking Lot",
        "estimated_damage_amount": 3172,
        "police_report_number": "PR-20250911-9821"
    }
} 




    }"]

["{

"claim_text": "A pipe burst Friday evening—September 12th—and the water soaked through the basement walls. It was a nightmare. My wife thought it was a leak from the washing machine, but when we called the plumber, he said no, it’s the upstairs bathroom line. They’ve already given a ballpark repair cost: $12,187. The agent yesterday said to call back today so it’s logged in the system properly. No police report filed—it wasn’t that type of incident. But I do have contractor documentation if you need it."

}"]

